# Build context of every image (docker build -f docker/<name>.Dockerfile . ; compose `build: context: .`). The
# Dockerfiles build from sources, so local build output, dependencies, VCS data and private or secret files never
# belong in it: they only slow the build, and some break it (a symlinked web/node_modules replaces the one `npm ci`
# installed) or leak into an image (a local server/build.properties or .env). Never list a tracked file here.
.git
**/node_modules
**/target
web/dist
web/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo
agent-android/.gradle
agent-android/.kotlin
agent-android/**/build
agent-android/local.properties
server/build.properties
# Legacy AngularJS console output (grunt/bower): webapp/lib would otherwise be packaged into ROOT.war.
server/src/main/webapp/lib
server/webtarget
**/bower_components
# Local dev-run base directory (rotated logs), wherever a run left it.
**/_BASE_DIRECTORY_
reference
brain
.claude
.superpowers
.idea
**/*.iml
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
**/*.log
**/*.bak
**/*.orig
**/*.swp
**/*~
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.apk
**/*.aab
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
